"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nUsing v4.3.stable.mono.official [77dcf97d8]\n\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu Linux 24.04.02 LTS, NVIDIA GeForce GTX 960\n\n### Issue description\n\nGetting an error when I try to add a TreeItem to the selected TreeItem using C#\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI have a Tree in my scene. In `_Ready()` I do:\n\n```c#\n_accountTree = GetNode<Tree>(\"Tree\");\n\t\t\nTreeItem rootTreeItem = _accountTree.CreateItem();\nrootTreeItem.SetText(0, \"Root\");\n\nTreeItem treeItem = _accountTree.CreateItem(rootTreeItem);\ntreeItem.SetText(0, \"Child 1\");\n\nTreeItem treeItem = _accountTree.CreateItem(rootTreeItem);\ntreeItem.SetText(0, \"Child 2\");\n```\n\n\nIn the godot editor, I set the Tree node to connect the `item_selected() `signal to the method `_OnTreeItemSelected()`\n\nThe want here is when one selects an item in the tree, it adds a child to it.\n\n```c#\npublic void _OnTreeItemSelected() {\n    TreeItem selectedTreeItem = _accountTree.GetSelected();\n\n    TreeItem treeItem = _accountTree.CreateItem(selectedTreeItem);\n    treeItem.SetText(0, \"Another Child\");\n```\n\n\n...\n\nOn the SetText line I get the error \" Exception of type` 'System.NullReferenceException' was thrown: Object reference not set to an instance of an object.\"`\n\nUsing the debugger I can see that selectedTreeItem is a TreeItem and does seem like it is the correct one (based on the name).\n\nMaybe one shouldn't be able to be able to add a child on the fly like this? Or perhaps that is a good use case but I am just doing it wrong?\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nIncluded in \"steps to reproduce\"","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.co